From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] luci-app-internet-detector: options of the new checks, latency
Requires: 001-check-fixes-ip-version-outbound-check 002-public-ip-dns-ipv6-providers

- Main settings: check type "sing-box outbound (Clash API)" with its
  options; the list of outbounds is read from the Clash API by the new
  rpcd method luci.internet-detector ClashProxies (address and secret
  of the first instance with this check, or of homeproxy). IP version,
  HTTP method and "Any HTTP response" for the other checks. Suggested
  values for hosts and URLs.
- Public IP: the new providers, a custom URL, IP version IPv4 / IPv6 /
  IPv4 + IPv6 for all providers.
- Status (page and overview): a card per instance with its state,
  description, latency, public IP, reason of a failure and time of the
  last check; the address is no longer passed through the translation
  function. Button "Check again": the new rpcd method Restart (write
  ACL) stops the instances and starts them again ("Web UI only") or
  restarts the service.
- Outbounds: homeproxy routing nodes by name and node labels next to
  their tags (rpcd ClashProxies reads them from /etc/config/homeproxy).
- Public IP: fallback provider; the network that serves each provider in
  its title. Device: a note that a device breaks the connections to a
  transparent proxy on the router.
- Russian translation of the new strings.

